{"id": "EUVD-2026-94404", "enisaUuid": "de455326-50e4-3a66-98c2-b7b91fb4a5cd", "description": "Gophish 0.11.0 through 0.12.1 contains a server-side request forgery vulnerability that allows authenticated low-privileged users to reach loopback and private hosts via POST /api/import/site. Attackers can submit internal URLs, which the default dialer deny list does not block, to read service responses and enumerate internal hosts and ports through error messages.", "datePublished": "2026-10-07T15:44:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-07T20:43:00", "baseScore": 5.3, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:L/UI:N/VC:L/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://blog.ostorlab.co/gophish-0121-manual-review-agentic-deep-scan.html", "https://github.com/gophish/gophish/blob/b1648f0759c6d57ac989157c55d8b47c40254fe6/dialer/dialer.go#L82-L86", "https://github.com/gophish/gophish/blob/b1648f0759c6d57ac989157c55d8b47c40254fe6/controllers/api/import.go#L102-L125", "https://github.com/gophish/gophish", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/gophish-0.11.0-through-0.12.1-ssrf-via-post-api-import-site"], "aliases": ["GHSA-5724-58m3-c7r6", "CVE-2026-107273"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.2, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "abadabd9-cac5-36c1-9494-6d4f00a87305", "product": {"name": "gophish", "vendor": {"name": "Gophish"}}, "product_version": "0.11.0 \u22640.12.1"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "c467445c-d7be-3241-82e6-3b874f2ce184", "vendor": {"name": "Gophish"}}], "isExploited": false}